        "date_published": "2026-06-05T10:43:28+00:00",
        "description": "<p>I got really tired, as a human, of parsing the standard marketing heavy web we have today.\nI've always loved the simplicity of gopher and gemini web.<p>Recently I found myself manually adding `/llm.txt` to most websites I visit because I find the content for LLMs strait to the point and clear. \nThe only annoyance is web browsers like chrome do not render the markdown.<p>So could the AI revolution actually fix the web for humans as a side effect?<p>Do you find yourself doing the same?</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48410589\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48410589</a></p>\n<p>Points: 10</p>\n<p># Comments: 9</p>",
